  {
   "id": 508715,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Factor <span data-math=\"x^{2} + 6x + 8\">x^{2} + 6x + 8</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\left( x + 2 \\right)\\left( x + 4 \\right)\">\\left( x + 2 \\right)\\left( x + 4 \\right)</span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"{x^2} + 6x + 8\"></span></p>\n<p>Look for factors of 8 that add up to 6. This works when the coefficient of the <span data-math=\"{x^2}\"></span> term is 1.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Factors of 8</td>\n<td>Sum of Factors = 6</td>\n<td>Success?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1 times 8</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"1 + 8 = 9\"></span></td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 times 4</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"2 + 4 = 6\"></span></td>\n<td>Yes!</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Because 2 and 4 are factors of 8 and they add up to 6, you can make the factors of the polynomial.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(x + 2)(x + 4)\"></span></p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
